WEBVTT

00:01.480 --> 00:03.480
TS

00:18.990 --> 00:23.960
Paris

00:39.140 --> 00:42.680
"Galerie du Roy"
The King's Gallery

00:46.440 --> 00:48.650
How's your grandpa?

00:48.650 --> 00:51.150
He's doing much better than before!

00:51.150 --> 00:52.820
That's good to hear.

01:24.230 --> 01:24.850
Yune.

01:26.230 --> 01:27.230
Yes!

01:28.150 --> 01:31.980
Isn't this country very different from your own?

01:31.980 --> 01:36.740
A shopping district like this is called a <i>Galerie</i> in France.

01:36.740 --> 01:38.360
<i>Galerie...</i>

01:43.660 --> 01:45.290
Do you want another?

02:20.700 --> 02:26.080
saa tobira wo ake machi e yuku

02:20.700 --> 02:26.080
さあ扉を開け街へ行く

02:20.700 --> 02:26.080
As I open the gate and step out into the street

02:26.700 --> 02:30.750
asa no hikari ga mabushii

02:26.700 --> 02:30.750
朝の光が眩しい

02:26.700 --> 02:30.750
I can see the sun shining brightly

02:33.750 --> 02:38.760
doko kara ka nagareru hanauta ni

02:33.750 --> 02:38.760
どこからか流れる鼻歌に

02:33.750 --> 02:38.760
I can hear humming in the distance

02:39.930 --> 02:43.680
kokoro hazumi tokete yuku

02:39.930 --> 02:43.680
心弾み解けてゆく

02:39.930 --> 02:43.680
It moves me and melts my heart

02:46.890 --> 02:52.360
mabuta tojireba ukabu egao

02:46.890 --> 02:52.360
瞼閉じれば浮かぶ笑顔

02:46.890 --> 02:52.360
I can see that smile when I close my eyes

02:53.520 --> 02:58.940
omoidasu tabi ni namida hitotsu

02:53.520 --> 02:58.940
思い出す度に涙ひとつ

02:53.520 --> 02:58.940
It brings me to tears whenever I remember it

02:59.450 --> 03:02.570
te wo hiroge hashiridase

02:59.450 --> 03:02.570
手を広げ 走りだせ

02:59.450 --> 03:02.570
Spread your arms out and take off

03:02.570 --> 03:05.910
hi no ataru toori wo

03:02.570 --> 03:05.910
陽の当たる 通りを

03:02.570 --> 03:05.910
Down the streets where the lights shine

03:05.910 --> 03:12.460
michiyuku hito ni genki ni aisatsu

03:05.910 --> 03:12.460
道行く人に 元気に挨拶

03:05.910 --> 03:12.460
Cheerfully greet people walking down the city streets

03:12.460 --> 03:19.090
atarashii kimochi de shinkokyuu shitara

03:12.460 --> 03:19.090
新しい 気持ちで深呼吸したら

03:12.460 --> 03:19.090
Take a deep breath to refresh yourself

03:19.090 --> 03:27.600
kono sekai wa hora itsudemo kimi no mono

03:19.090 --> 03:27.600
この世界はほら いつでも 君のもの

03:19.090 --> 03:27.600
And this world will always be yours

03:32.940 --> 03:43.030
Episode 01 :

03:32.940 --> 03:43.030
" Entry "

03:47.280 --> 03:50.870
"Enseignes du Roy"
The King's Signs

04:02.340 --> 04:04.510
Sorry, I-

04:04.510 --> 04:05.970
Grandpa!

04:06.390 --> 04:08.720
You're always so aloof.

04:08.720 --> 04:10.890
You'll lose customers if you keep that up.

04:11.310 --> 04:13.600
The purchase in Japan was a success.

04:14.060 --> 04:16.610
These are some of the spoils from the war.

04:20.730 --> 04:23.650
That's great and all, but what is that...

04:28.700 --> 04:32.290
Is that <i>Japonaise</i> part of the spoils, too?

04:32.500 --> 04:38.290
Yune here was sent to be a live-in maid by her family.

04:38.290 --> 04:41.210
She said she wanted to work in Paris, so I brought her here.

04:41.210 --> 04:42.130
What?!

04:42.130 --> 04:43.380
She bent her hip!

04:43.380 --> 04:44.800
This is called a bow.

04:48.430 --> 04:53.180
Grandpa, I don't mind some souvenirs, since they can be profitable,

04:53.180 --> 05:00.320
but you can't forget that we're a metal crafts store, <i>Enseignes du Roy</i> !

05:00.320 --> 05:04.530
Don't worry. We also make signs.

05:04.530 --> 05:07.530
Metal craft for lights in Japan is very interesting.

05:07.820 --> 05:11.160
These <i>Chochin</i> function as signs.

05:11.160 --> 05:13.120
That's not what I mean.

05:13.120 --> 05:17.000
I meant that a sign store doesn't need a <i>Japonaise</i>,

05:17.000 --> 05:20.170
and we don't even have enough time or money to keep a maid.

05:20.420 --> 05:24.260
Don't worry. Yune eats like a bird.

05:24.260 --> 05:28.970
She was also the most popular sign in Nagasaki.

05:28.970 --> 05:33.560
Employees who are adept at calling in customers are called Sign Girls in Japan.

05:34.180 --> 05:36.940
Claude is the owner of this store, Yune.

05:36.940 --> 05:38.520
Say hello.

05:39.650 --> 05:40.650
Okay!

05:47.780 --> 05:52.580
My name is Yune, Master.

05:53.700 --> 05:54.370
Wha-

05:54.370 --> 05:56.370
Are you some kind of pervert, Grandpa?!

05:56.370 --> 05:59.250
It's wrong to make her do such a slave-like pose!

05:59.250 --> 06:02.380
No, Claude! That's a normal Japanese greeting!

06:02.380 --> 06:05.260
It's a very versatile pose that can be used as an apology or for giving thanks!

06:05.260 --> 06:06.130
No!

06:07.930 --> 06:13.930
I'm disappointed that you cannot appreciate the wonders of Japan.

06:14.390 --> 06:17.520
This man is inherently cranky, Yune.

06:17.520 --> 06:18.980
Don't worry too much about him.

06:18.980 --> 06:19.650
All right.

06:19.650 --> 06:21.400
Don't teach her strange things!

06:21.400 --> 06:26.860
Don't worry. The only French she knows is how to introduce herself.

06:27.360 --> 06:32.410
Does that mean Yune is responding without knowing what you're saying?

06:32.410 --> 06:35.620
She is very good at understanding the atmosphere.

06:35.620 --> 06:40.420
She'll nod to just about anything.

06:42.040 --> 06:43.920
How can you be fine with that?

06:45.130 --> 06:46.760
You don't understand the language,

06:46.760 --> 06:48.260
you blindly serve the people,

06:48.260 --> 06:50.470
and you can't even share your own thoughts.

06:50.470 --> 06:52.180
I wouldn't be able to deal with that.

06:52.180 --> 06:56.810
I really can't understand Yune and her people.

06:56.810 --> 06:58.100
Claude...

06:58.100 --> 07:01.350
Yune can't understand anything I'm saying, right?

07:11.820 --> 07:14.120
This is going to be your room from now on.

07:14.120 --> 07:15.990
Use it any way you want.

07:16.910 --> 07:17.660
Okay.

07:18.200 --> 07:21.080
I know! I'll give you something nice.

07:23.670 --> 07:27.670
Oscar-sama! Are you a magician?

07:27.670 --> 07:28.920
A magician?

07:28.920 --> 07:30.630
I'm surprised you knew that word.

07:30.630 --> 07:31.550
Keep this a secret.

07:36.260 --> 07:38.520
Take a seat, Yune.

08:01.460 --> 08:04.710
This is <i>my</i> precious workshop.

08:04.710 --> 08:06.880
Don't interrupt my work.

08:06.880 --> 08:08.880
Yes, Claude-sama.

09:31.750 --> 09:32.800
What?

09:35.510 --> 09:37.010
It's so pretty.

09:37.010 --> 09:39.260
It's a butterfly!

09:39.600 --> 09:40.850
Don't touch it.

09:40.850 --> 09:43.060
I just finished repairing it.

09:46.940 --> 09:50.940
This is the last thing my father ever made.

09:50.940 --> 09:54.360
Did you see the sign at the entrance of the <i>Galerie</i>?

09:54.650 --> 10:00.160
That was made upon request by my father and grandpa, who used to be blacksmiths.

10:00.740 --> 10:04.700
This store has been here ever since that sign was put at the front of the <i>Galerie</i>,

10:05.580 --> 10:07.210
along with the secondhand clothing shop next door,

10:07.210 --> 10:09.420
and even the printer next to that.

10:09.420 --> 10:13.710
All of the signs in the <i>Galerie</i> were made by the three generations of blacksmiths.

10:14.380 --> 10:17.720
They're proof of our finesse, and we're very proud of them.

10:18.590 --> 10:25.430
There used to be a big <i>atelier</i> nearby, and they used to do a lot of work for the <i>Galerie</i> as well,

10:25.430 --> 10:29.100
including lights, chandeliers, and facades.

10:30.270 --> 10:35.980
Well, my father is dead now and my grandpa can't work anymore.

10:36.820 --> 10:40.860
Not to mention <i>Galerie du Roy</i> is having financial difficulties.

10:40.860 --> 10:43.080
This is a very important time for us.

10:43.990 --> 10:48.330
Our fifty-year legacy is contained here.

10:48.580 --> 10:53.500
I need to keep this store going, even if I have to do it alone.

10:53.500 --> 10:57.340
I guess you wouldn't understand that, though.

10:57.340 --> 10:58.510
Yune!

10:59.550 --> 11:02.760
The workshop and the store are both spotless!

11:02.760 --> 11:05.600
Isn't she a very hard worker?

11:07.680 --> 11:10.060
Well, since she's a Sign Girl,

11:10.770 --> 11:14.360
you should go up to the front of the store...

11:14.360 --> 11:18.320
I know! Remember that beautiful <i>kimono</i> that you showed me?

11:18.320 --> 11:20.200
You should wear it and hold a <i>Chochin</i> and-

11:20.200 --> 11:21.200
Grandpa.

11:22.030 --> 11:25.370
Oh? I thought she was a doll.

11:26.740 --> 11:29.040
How rare.

11:29.040 --> 11:30.250
Is she a <i>Japonaise</i>?

11:30.250 --> 11:33.460
No wonder she looks like a doll!

11:33.460 --> 11:35.040
Uh- Um...

11:35.040 --> 11:36.960
She's no doll.

11:36.960 --> 11:39.380
Now, please get out.

11:40.300 --> 11:41.590
R-Right.

11:44.640 --> 11:45.760
See?

11:45.760 --> 11:48.560
Sign Girls are very effective.

11:49.560 --> 11:53.940
By the way, you're still awful at sales.

11:53.940 --> 11:58.570
That man would've probably bought some souvenirs from Japan.

12:33.640 --> 12:34.770
Don't touch it!

12:36.650 --> 12:38.020
You'll just get hurt.

12:42.440 --> 12:44.660
I am deeply sorry!

12:45.410 --> 12:49.160
You should really just go back to Japan as soon as you can.

12:50.290 --> 12:55.170
I don't blame you, but you just couldn't be our sign,

12:55.170 --> 12:59.590
just like how those long sleeves serve no purpose in France.

13:00.000 --> 13:01.840
I am deeply sorry.

13:02.340 --> 13:03.880
Claude...

13:04.130 --> 13:05.840
I know.

13:05.840 --> 13:08.350
I don't know enough about Yune.

13:08.350 --> 13:13.730
But Yune doesn't know enough about this place, either.

13:21.360 --> 13:23.400
Doesn't it smell wonderful?

13:23.400 --> 13:24.240
Which one do you want?

13:24.240 --> 13:25.860
Oh, my!

13:53.350 --> 13:55.640
Let's have dinner, Yune.

13:56.100 --> 13:58.230
Will the sign be okay?

13:58.230 --> 14:02.610
Don't worry. Claude may be rude, but he's very skilled.

14:07.450 --> 14:09.820
Help yourself, Yune.

14:29.220 --> 14:30.260
Yune.

14:31.140 --> 14:31.930
Y-Yes?

14:36.100 --> 14:37.980
You don't need to do that.

14:38.350 --> 14:40.060
The sign is fixed now.

14:42.610 --> 14:45.070
Will it be like it used to?

14:45.070 --> 14:47.690
I'll apologize to the custo-

14:47.030 --> 14:47.690
No,

14:48.780 --> 14:52.160
apologies can't fix everything.

14:54.120 --> 14:57.950
Besides, glass has to break sometime.

14:58.580 --> 15:01.420
This design isn't too bad, either.

15:01.420 --> 15:03.090
So, don't worry.

15:03.750 --> 15:05.500
I'm going to go set this up.

15:06.090 --> 15:07.590
You should go to sleep.

15:07.590 --> 15:08.920
You must be tired.

15:25.360 --> 15:26.820
Claude-sama!

15:28.400 --> 15:30.320
Um, please take this.

15:30.530 --> 15:31.700
A <i>kimono</i>?

15:32.280 --> 15:33.700
Is that some sort of compensation?

15:36.450 --> 15:38.620
It's expensive, right?

15:38.620 --> 15:40.120
You don't have to-

15:45.540 --> 15:51.380
Fine. If you say so, I'll have it sold during the Art Gallery which ordered this sign.

16:07.520 --> 16:11.030
You've restored your father's design quite nicely.

16:11.030 --> 16:11.740
Huh?

16:12.320 --> 16:13.820
The wings seem a bit different.

16:13.820 --> 16:15.820
That's <i>my</i> little piece of art.

16:16.120 --> 16:17.410
It isn't bad, is it?

16:17.410 --> 16:19.040
No, it's good.

16:19.040 --> 16:19.950
Isn't it?

16:20.450 --> 16:24.080
By the way, Claude, I was wondering...

16:24.540 --> 16:27.420
Where did you get that strange fabric?

16:28.460 --> 16:29.500
That?

16:33.380 --> 16:36.390
THE LITTLE BEES

16:43.600 --> 16:44.810
Claude-sama!

16:44.810 --> 16:46.310
You were waiting for me?

16:47.400 --> 16:49.150
Here, take this.

16:52.360 --> 16:55.570
It's a children's book I just bought.

16:56.780 --> 16:58.580
Claude...

16:58.580 --> 17:02.250
That's probably the best thing to use if you want to learn French.

17:04.620 --> 17:07.460
Thank you very much.

17:27.810 --> 17:28.810
This is...

17:28.770 --> 17:33.070
Sold

17:29.520 --> 17:31.190
Yune's <i>kimono</i>...?

17:31.190 --> 17:32.480
Why is it here?

17:33.070 --> 17:35.150
Sold

17:33.610 --> 17:35.200
Sold?

17:35.400 --> 17:37.450
Hey, I have a question about this <i>kimono</i>.

17:37.450 --> 17:39.120
Hello, Oscar-san!

17:39.120 --> 17:39.950
Thank you!

17:39.950 --> 17:41.950
I was able to sell it at an exceptionally high price.

17:41.950 --> 17:43.700
You sold it?

17:45.080 --> 17:46.160
Hey, Claude!

17:47.330 --> 17:49.170
Did you sell Yune's <i>kimono</i>?!

17:49.170 --> 17:50.840
Yeah. Didn't you hear?

17:50.840 --> 17:52.000
500 francs!

17:52.000 --> 17:54.170
This is all thanks to Yune!

17:54.170 --> 17:55.170
Claude!

17:55.420 --> 17:56.720
Wh-What?

17:57.880 --> 18:01.930
That was Yune's most expensive <i>kimono</i>,

18:01.930 --> 18:03.720
and it was a memento of her mother.

18:03.970 --> 18:05.520
A memento?

18:06.100 --> 18:08.850
But Yune gave it to me willingly.

18:12.820 --> 18:13.730
Yune!

18:15.860 --> 18:17.150
Claude-sama?

18:17.450 --> 18:20.240
Was that <i>kimono</i> really your mother's memento?!

18:24.120 --> 18:25.540
So it was.

18:27.410 --> 18:28.620
I'll go get it back.

18:28.620 --> 18:29.460
No!

18:29.460 --> 18:30.380
Wait!

18:30.830 --> 18:32.340
Please!

18:32.340 --> 18:36.340
That would be bad for the signs!

18:37.340 --> 18:40.260
Signs show credence in Japan!

18:40.590 --> 18:45.970
When you take the <i>kimono</i> back, you and people in the <i>Galerie</i> will lose credence!

18:45.970 --> 18:49.020
I don't want that to happen!

18:53.770 --> 18:57.110
You understood what I was saying?

18:57.110 --> 19:01.740
<i>I really can't understand Yune and her people.</i>

19:01.950 --> 19:05.040
<i>Yune can't understand anything I'm saying, right?</i>

19:05.240 --> 19:08.960
<i>You should really just go back to Japan as soon as you can.</i>

19:11.500 --> 19:13.080
<i>Um, please, take this.</i>

19:14.840 --> 19:16.590
Why would you go this far?

19:18.380 --> 19:25.720
I am here to serve Claude-sama and <i>Galerie du Roy</i>, which he loves.

19:26.180 --> 19:31.350
I want to be part of this <i>Galerie</i>'s family.

19:37.360 --> 19:40.110
This is the first time you've spoken for yourself.

19:40.820 --> 19:44.780
So you knew how to speak the whole time.

19:45.580 --> 19:46.580
I am deeply-

19:45.870 --> 19:46.580
Stop.

19:47.410 --> 19:50.080
I'm the one who needs to apologize.

20:02.430 --> 20:08.930
I don't know much about your people, but I can feel your will.

20:09.470 --> 20:13.980
I will buy that <i>kimono</i> back at many times the price one day.

20:14.730 --> 20:22.570
Could you be the judge of my trustworthiness until that time comes?

20:24.700 --> 20:26.990
Y-Yes.

20:28.580 --> 20:29.740
Good.

20:29.740 --> 20:30.870
It's a promise.

20:34.620 --> 20:37.590
In exchange, I need you to make a promise as well.

20:37.590 --> 20:39.130
A promise?

20:39.460 --> 20:43.590
Don't get rid of your precious things ever again.

20:47.180 --> 20:48.050
Okay!

20:54.020 --> 20:57.360
Paris. The end of the 19th century.

20:57.690 --> 21:01.110
Beneath the glass ceiling of the <i>Galerie du Roy</i>,

21:01.320 --> 21:06.990
One can see the thin silhouette of a Japanese girl named Yune.

21:07.660 --> 21:13.410
For now, only a few Parisians know of her arrival.

21:23.090 --> 21:29.680
aa marude yume wo miteru you na

21:23.090 --> 21:29.680
ああ、まるで夢を見てるような

21:23.090 --> 21:29.680
Ah, it's as if I'm in a dream

21:29.680 --> 21:35.480
yawarakana hikari no naka de

21:29.680 --> 21:35.480
柔らかな光の中で

21:29.680 --> 21:35.480
As I lie here in this tender light

21:35.480 --> 21:46.490
me wo tojite mimi wo sumasereba kikoete kuru

21:35.480 --> 21:46.490
目を閉じて耳を澄ませれば　聞こえてくる

21:35.480 --> 21:46.490
When I close my eyes and listen, I can hear it

21:48.320 --> 22:01.380
atatakaku watashi wo yobu yasashii sono koe ga

21:48.320 --> 22:01.380
あたたかく私を呼ぶ優しいその声が

21:48.320 --> 22:01.380
That kind voice that warmly calls to me

22:03.960 --> 22:10.550
afureru omoi wo tsutaetai kono te kara

22:03.960 --> 22:10.550
溢れる思いを伝えたい　この手から

22:03.960 --> 22:10.550
I want to extend my feelings with these hands

22:10.550 --> 22:16.850
kotoba ja nakute kokoro de tsunagaru

22:10.550 --> 22:16.850
言葉じゃなくて　心で繋がる

22:10.550 --> 22:16.850
We connect through our hearts, not our words

22:16.850 --> 22:23.530
hajimeyou koko kara sodateyou nukumori wo

22:16.850 --> 22:23.530
始めよう　ここから育てよう　温もりを

22:16.850 --> 22:23.530
Let's begin here. Let's nurture the warmth

22:23.530 --> 22:29.990
atarashii hibi ga watashi wo matteru

22:23.530 --> 22:29.990
新しい日々が私を待ってる

22:23.530 --> 22:29.990
A new day is waiting for me

22:29.990 --> 22:43.710
mamoru mono wa kitto koko ni aru no

22:29.990 --> 22:43.710
守るものはきっとここにあるの

22:29.990 --> 22:43.710
I'm sure there is something here for me to protect

22:50.550 --> 22:53.010
A: Abeille (bee)

22:53.010 --> 22:55.640
B: Bonbon (candy)

22:55.640 --> 22:58.100
C: Chèvre (goat)

22:58.100 --> 23:00.520
E: Enseigne (sign)

23:01.270 --> 23:06.860
Oh yeah, Yune. If you know French, then you shouldn't need that book.

23:06.860 --> 23:12.490
I promised that I wouldn't get rid of my precious things!

23:13.780 --> 23:16.740
She could end up being pretty stubborn.

23:35.140 --> 24:00.870
Episode 02 :

23:35.140 --> 24:00.870
" Cheese "

23:35.220 --> 23:36.350
Next episode:

23:36.350 --> 23:37.470
"Cheese".

